[1.085351, "o", "\r\n"]
[1.805885, "o", "Initialized mnema project at ~/your-repository/.mnema\r\n  identity: mnid:22d03c71c66022aff6fc386f2d39f6c0819638847d0e932bf9289f5b6ed54b35\r\n"]
[1.805958, "o", "  backup key: created and enrolled — private half at ~/.mnema/identity/backup/c6d1d0e32b7803f67022f53d36c207b5e60c2152385e454c516a2964f461c12b.key\r\n  Move that file off this machine: a backup left on this disk is lost with it.\r\n"]
[1.805978, "o", "\r\n"]
[1.806152, "o", "  mnema writes no file of yours. In Claude Code the mnema plugin hands this record to\r\n  each session on its own. Without it, `mnema brief > MNEMA.md` puts what governs this\r\n"]
[1.806179, "o", "  project in a file of its own — the `>` replaces the whole of the file it names — and\r\n  one line in a `CLAUDE.md` brings that file in (an `AGENTS.md` is read there only\r\n  where no `CLAUDE.md` exists):\r\n    @MNEMA.md\r\n"]
[1.806269, "o", "\r\n  Commit `.mnema/` with the repository: the record travels with it, and every clone reads it.\r\n  Next: `mnema decision record <title> <rationale>`; `mnema status` shows where things stand.\r\n"]
[3.428233, "o", "\u001b[2m# write down a call, with the reasoning and what was turned down\u001b[0m\r\n"]
